# Commercial S12.1 absent-unit rollback diagnosis

- Scope: pre-freeze review of rollback before first unit installation.
- Finding: `systemctl show` with strict checking could abort rollback when the
  S12.1 unit legitimately did not exist in the pre-state.
- Correction: a structured state query recognizes only explicit systemd
  `not-found`/“unit could not be found” as `inactive/dead`; any other query
  failure remains fail-closed. Active units still require successful stop and
  verified `inactive/dead` before restoration.
- Regression proof: explicit missing-unit and unrelated-error paths are tested.
- Runtime effect: none; the one permitted server attempt remains unused.
